# hook-pre-build - Entry point for pre-build hook
#
# Runs user's hook script before build starts, after tooling validation.
# Use this hook for environment setup, custom tool installation, or early
# preparation that should happen before quality checks and versioning.
#
# This hook runs BEFORE versions-and-naming - version outputs are NOT available.
# PROJECT_NAME and IS_RELEASE are calculated inline for convenience.
#
# Inputs (environment variables):
#   HOOK_PRE_BUILD_SCRIPT_SUB_PATH - Path to user's hook script
#
# Available context (set by CI wrapper):
#   PROJECT_NAME - Repository name (calculated inline)
#   IS_RELEASE - Whether this is a release build (calculated inline)
#   REPOSITORY_NAME - Raw repository name (from CI provider)
#   REPOSITORY_OWNER - Repository owner (from CI provider)
#   CURRENT_BRANCH - Current branch name (PR head ref, or ref name for direct pushes)
#   DEFAULT_BRANCH - Repository default branch
#   OUTPUT_SUB_PATH - Build output directory (default: kaptain-out)
#   DOCKERFILE_SUB_PATH - Docker source directory (default: src/docker)
#   MANIFESTS_SUB_PATH - Manifests source directory (default: src/kubernetes)
#   CONFIG_SUB_PATH - Config files directory (default: src/config)
#   ... and all other workflow inputs
#
# NOT available at this lifecycle point:
#   VERSION, VERSION_*, DOCKER_TAG, GIT_TAG, DOCKER_IMAGE_NAME
#
set -euo pipefail

